<SiteLayout title="Sonya Hair Braiding | Meta Ads &amp; Booking Case Study" description="Meta lead generation for a Harlem salon: 256 form leads at $2.13, 94 Meta-reported call actions at $5.18, plus funnel and CRM infrastructure." path="/work/sonya-hair-braiding/">
<article class="case-study">
<header class="case-hero"><div class="case-container"><p class="case-kicker"><a href="/work/">Selected Work</a> / Meta Ads / Local Lead Generation</p>
<h1>Generating leads and calls for a Harlem hair braiding salon.</h1>
<p class="case-lede">For Sonya African Hair Braiding, LeadsFlo combined Facebook and Instagram lead-generation campaigns with a dedicated funnel, call tracking, HighLevel CRM and appointment-booking infrastructure.</p>
<div class="case-tags"><span>Meta Ads</span><span>Instant Forms</span><span>Call Campaigns</span><span>HighLevel CRM</span><span>Booking Funnel</span></div><a class="case-btn" href="/contact/">Discuss your lead generation ↗</a></div></header>
<section class="case-container"><figure class="case-media"><img src="/work/sonya-hair-braiding.webp" alt="Sonya African Hair Braiding landing page with inquiry questionnaire" fetchpriority="high"/><figcaption>Dedicated salon landing page and hairstyle qualification funnel.</figcaption></figure></section>
<section class="case-band"><div class="case-container"><p class="case-overline">Campaign reporting / October 24, 2026</p><h2>Measured interest from two conversion paths.</h2>
<div class="case-stats"><div class="case-stat"><strong>256</strong><span>Meta Instant Form leads</span></div><div class="case-stat"><strong>$2.13</strong><span>Cost per form lead</span></div><div class="case-stat"><strong>94</strong><span>Meta-reported call actions</span></div><div class="case-stat"><strong>$5.18</strong><span>Cost per call action</span></div></div>
<p><strong>$1,031.66</strong> total reported spend across both campaigns ($544.71 lead forms; $486.95 call campaign), with 55,358 combined impressions.</p>
<p class="case-note">Form leads and call actions are different metrics. Call actions are not confirmed answered calls or booked appointments. No verified appointment count, attributable revenue or return on ad spend is claimed.</p><figure class="case-media"><img loading="lazy" src="/work/sonya-hair-meta-ads.png" alt="Meta Ads Manager campaign results showing lead and call campaign reporting for Sonya Hair Braiding"/><figcaption>Campaign reporting screenshot, October 24, 2026. The metrics below distinguish submitted forms from Meta-reported call actions.</figcaption></figure></div></section>
<section class="case-band case-alt"><div class="case-container"><div class="case-intro"><p class="case-overline">The business challenge</p><h2>More inquiries meant nothing without follow-up.</h2><p>The Harlem salon wanted more potential customers, an organized way to capture hairstyle preferences and a reliable route from inquiry to appointment. Missed calls and inconsistent follow-up were practical constraints, so the work extended beyond ad delivery.</p></div><div class="case-grid">
<div class="case-card"><span class="case-n">01 / META INSTANT FORMS</span><h3>Lower-friction inquiries.</h3><p>Lead forms collected braid style, desired length and size, previous experience and contact information. Ads emphasized real hairstyle examples, Harlem location, 24/7 availability and advertised pricing from $180.</p></div>
<div class="case-card"><span class="case-n">02 / DIRECT-CALL ADS</span><h3>Another way to respond.</h3><p>Call-focused campaigns gave prospects a direct route to the salon. A dedicated HighLevel number forwarded calls to the business and recorded inbound activity.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section class="case-band"><div class="case-container"><p class="case-overline">The booking system</p><h2>A structured three-step customer journey.</h2><div class="case-grid case-grid-three">
<div class="case-card"><span class="case-n">01 / DISCOVER</span><h3>Landing page.</h3><p>Show relevant braid styles, present the offer and collect customer preferences through a guided inquiry experience.</p></div>
<div class="case-card"><span class="case-n">02 / CHOOSE</span><h3>Calendar request.</h3><p>Visitors select a preferred date and time; their request connects to HighLevel's appointment calendar.</p></div>
<div class="case-card"><span class="case-n">03 / CONFIRM</span><h3>Thank-you page.</h3><p>Visitors receive next-step guidance and are encouraged to confirm hairstyle details and availability with the salon.</p></div></div>
<div class="case-flow" style="margin-top:30px"><span>Facebook / Instagram</span><b>→</b><span>Lead / Call</span><b>→</b><span>CRM</span><b>→</b><span>Booking Request</span><b>→</b><span>Follow-up</span></div></div></section>
<section class="case-band case-alt"><div class="case-container"><p class="case-overline">Built beyond the advertisements</p><h2>Connected infrastructure for lead handling.</h2><div class="case-grid">
<div class="case-card"><h3>CRM and tracking</h3><p>HighLevel configuration centralized contact records, customer conversations, call activity, pipelines and appointment requests. The account contained 468 contacts in the October 24 snapshot; this is not a count of new Meta leads.</p></div>
<div class="case-card"><h3>Follow-up and automations</h3><p>Lead notifications, booking communications, reminders and missed-call follow-up workflows were configured. We distinguish configured infrastructure from confirmed production outcomes.</p></div>
</div><p class="case-note">The CRM tracking number was at one stage also listed on organic social profiles. That limits reliable attribution of some inbound calls to paid versus organic traffic. Customer contact records are intentionally not displayed here.</p></div></section>
<section class="case-band"><div class="case-container"><p class="case-overline">What the project taught us</p><h2>Ad performance and business outcomes are different.</h2><p class="case-intro">The campaigns generated documented interest, but the salon also faced missed calls, delayed responses and inconsistent adoption of the follow-up systems. The next stage of growth depends on turning those opportunities into answered conversations and confirmed bookings.</p><div class="case-card"><h3>The practical takeaway</h3><p>Measure leads, call actions, answered calls, bookings and completed appointments separately. Improving acquisition is useful; improving the full lead-handling process is how businesses can turn it into sales opportunities.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="case-footer"><div class="case-container"><p class="case-overline">Connect marketing to follow-through</p><h2>Want more qualified inquiries—not just clicks?</h2><p>Let's discuss your advertising, lead capture, booking process and follow-up.</p><a class="case-btn" href="/contact/">Discuss your project ↗</a><div><a class="case-back" href="/work/">← All selected work</a></div></div></section>
</article>
</SiteLayout>
